@event evo_rain_barrel
# en: Rain on Demand
title [b62937] = 呼雨即来
# en: {Tidecalling at Evocation II. Pull a cloud off the lake, park it over a barrel, and fill the barrel to the chalk line. Not over, not under.|The barrels are out on the terrace again, each with a chalk line.|You know your barrel now, the one with the iron band that's slipped.} {Professor Marisol is reading on the steps, under a perfectly dry patch of air.|The wind keeps trying to borrow the clouds.|{season == "winter": The clouds come off the lake as sleet.|A heron watches the barrels with professional interest.}}
text [21af36] = {塑能术 II 的唤潮课。从湖上拽一朵云，停在木桶上方，把桶灌到粉笔线为止。不许多，也不许少。|木桶又摆上了露台，每只都画着粉笔线。|如今你认得自己的桶了，就是铁箍滑下来的那只。} {玛丽索尔教授坐在台阶上看书，头顶那一小块空气干干爽爽。|风一直想把云借走。|{season == "winter": 云从湖上过来，落下的是冻雨。|一只苍鹭以专业的兴趣盯着这些木桶。}}
# en: A row of students on a lakeside terrace, each with a small grey cloud above a wooden barrel, one cloud raining sideways onto a neighbour.
scene [c50d40] = 湖畔露台上站着一排学生，每人头顶一小朵灰云，下方是一只木桶，其中一朵云正斜着把雨下到邻座身上。
# en: Wring it out to the line
opt.left.label [0e4325] = 拧到粉笔线
# en: {The last drop lands on the chalk. Marisol looks up from her book and back down, which counts.|You stop the rain a breath early and let the drip finish the job. Exactly to the line.|You know how much your barrel leaks at the slipped band, and you rain that much extra. Exactly to the line.}
opt.left.say.1 [fe435c] = {最后一滴正好落在粉笔线上。玛丽索尔从书上抬眼看了看，又低下头去，这就算数了。|你提前一口气收住雨，让余滴把活干完。不多不少，正到线上。|你知道你那只桶在松脱的铁箍处漏多少，就多下那么多。不多不少，正到线上。}
# en: {Your cloud overshoots, fills the barrel, and keeps going down your collar.|The cloud drifts left and rains on the next barrel, which is not yours, and on its owner, who is very not yours. The splashback finds your collar anyway.|The heron moves at the wrong moment and so does your cloud. It empties itself over the heron, who leaves offended.}
opt.left.say.2 [e794c2] = {你的云下过了头，灌满木桶后接着往你衣领里灌。|云往左飘，下在了旁边的桶上，那不是你的桶，也下在了桶的主人身上，那更不是你的人。溅起的水还是找到了你的衣领。|苍鹭在不该动的时候动了，你的云也是。它把雨全倒在了苍鹭身上，苍鹭气呼呼地走了。}
# en: Drizzle it in, slowly
opt.right.label [b367cf] = 慢慢地洒进去
# en: {It takes the whole lesson. Your cloud is the size of a pillow by the end, and very tired.|You fill it a thimble at a time. The others have gone in for lunch. The line is met.|You drizzle it in while your barrel leaks it out at the band. It's a long lesson, but you win in the end.}
opt.right.say.1 [9eee07] = {这花了整整一节课。到最后你的云只剩枕头那么大，而且累坏了。|你一顶针一顶针地往里灌。别人都去吃午饭了。线终于到了。|你一点一点往里下，桶又从铁箍那儿一点一点往外漏。这节课很漫长，但最后你赢了。}

@event evo_ember_stair
# en: Carrying the Ember
title [5d68d8] = 掌中余火
# en: {Pyromancy at Evocation II. Carry a live ember in your bare palm from the ground floor to the top of the Lecture Tower. Keep it alight. Keep your hand.|The ember drill again. The stair hasn't got any shorter.|Ember day. You've counted the stair by now, and you know where the draught is.} {A door on the third floor opens just as you pass.|Someone ahead of you is climbing very fast and swearing quietly.|The lamps on the stair are out, and your ember is the only light.}
text [633df9] = {塑能术 II 的火焰术课。赤手托一块燃着的炭，从讲堂塔底层走到塔顶。别让它灭，也别丢了你的手。|又是托炭练习。楼梯并没有变短。|托炭日。你早数清了台阶，也知道穿堂风在哪儿。} {你经过时，三楼的一扇门恰好打开。|你前面有人爬得飞快，嘴里小声骂着。|楼梯上的灯全灭了，你掌心的炭是唯一的光。}
# en: A student climbing a dim spiral stair, a single glowing ember resting in their bare open palm.
scene [0a00df] = 一名学生在昏暗的螺旋楼梯上攀登，一块发光的余炭躺在摊开的赤裸掌心里。
# en: Feed it, and climb fast
opt.left.label [76bdf4] = 喂着火，快步上
# en: {You keep the ember bright with small breaths of heat and take the stairs two at a time. It arrives fat and orange.|You reach the top with the ember glowing and your palm only warm. The lecturer tips it into a brazier without a word.|Your ember lights the dark stair all the way up. People wait on the landings to follow you.}
opt.left.say.1 [ca1e10] = {你用细细的热息让炭保持明亮，一步跨两级台阶。到顶时它又胖又红。|你到达塔顶，炭还亮着，掌心只是温热。讲师一言不发地把它倒进火盆。|你的炭一路照亮了漆黑的楼梯。人们在平台上等着跟你走。}
# en: {The ember flares on the landing and you learn exactly how hot a palm can get. You arrive with it alight, and with a blister.|You feed it too much at the draughty window. It bites. You carry it up the last flight in your other hand.|You feed it in the dark and misjudge it. It bites, and you finish the climb by its light and your own swearing.}
opt.left.say.2 [2166ef] = {炭在楼梯平台上猛地一窜，你终于知道掌心能有多烫。到顶时它还燃着，你也多了个水泡。|在透风的窗边你喂得太多，它咬了你一口。最后一段楼梯，你换了只手托着它。|黑暗里你喂错了量。它咬了你一口，你借着它的光，骂骂咧咧地爬完了剩下的路。}
# en: Shield it, and climb slow
opt.right.label [d3a230] = 护着火，慢慢上
# en: {You climb at a crawl with the ember cupped against the draughts. It is alight at the top, just. So are your nerves.|Step by step, a held breath at each window. Last up, but the ember's still glowing.|You shield it from the draught you know is coming. It reaches the top small and steady, and so do you.}
opt.right.say.1 [216201] = {你一步一挪地往上爬，双手拢着炭挡风。到顶时它还亮着，勉强亮着。你的神经也是。|一步一步，每过一扇窗就屏一口气。你最后一个到，但炭还亮着。|你提前挡住了你知道会来的那股风。它到顶时小小的、稳稳的，你也是。}

@event evo_firebreak
# en: The Reed Burn
title [b50131] = 烧芦苇
# en: {Advanced Evocation does real work, the controlled burn of the dead reeds along the lake shore. Pyromancers lead the fire, tidecallers hold the line behind it.|Burn day. The shore smells of smoke for a week afterwards.|The reed burn. You can tell a fire's mood from its smoke now.} {The wind is steady from the lake.|The wind can't decide.|The reeds are drier than anyone would like.} {season == "summer": The air is hot already.|Your breath steams.}
text [9e6bd2] = {高等塑能术要干真活，湖岸那片枯芦苇的控制烧荒。火焰术的人领着火走，唤潮术的人在后面守线。|烧荒日。之后整整一周，湖岸都是烟味。|烧芦苇。如今你看烟就知道火的脾气。} {风从湖上稳稳地吹来。|风拿不定主意。|芦苇干得让谁都不放心。} {season == "summer": 空气已经很热了。|你呼出的气都成了白雾。}
# en: Advanced students along a lake shore in a line, half of them calling a low wall of fire through dry reeds, half of them holding back a curtain of lake water behind it.
scene [c4e483] = 高年级学生沿湖岸站成一排，一半人引着一道低矮的火墙穿过枯芦苇，另一半人在火墙后撑起一道湖水的帘幕。
# en: Walk at the fire's head
opt.left.label [13e32e] = 走在火头
# en: {The fire follows your hands down the shore like a dog on a lead. The lecturer lets you take it all the way to the boathouse.|You lead the fire low and even, and it goes out where you tell it. Behind you there's nothing but clean black ground.|You lead the fire through the dry reeds slowly and keep it on a short lead. Not a spark gets away.}
opt.left.say.1 [807c0c] = {火像牵着绳的狗，跟着你的手沿岸走。讲师让你一路把它带到船屋。|你把火领得又低又匀，它在你说停的地方熄灭。身后只剩干干净净的黑土。|你领着火慢慢穿过干芦苇，绳子收得很短。一颗火星都没逃掉。}
# en: {A gust lifts the fire over your head. The tidecallers drop it in a wall of lake water, and you with it.|The fire jumps the line and runs. It's caught in a minute, but your eyebrows weren't.|The dry reeds go up faster than you can lead them. The tidecallers save the boathouse; you save some of your sleeve.}
opt.left.say.2 [1c028e] = {一阵风把火掀过你头顶。唤潮术的人一道湖水墙把它压了下去，连你一起。|火越过了线，跑了起来。一分钟就被逮住了，你的眉毛却没逃掉。|干芦苇烧得比你领得还快。唤潮术的人保住了船屋，你保住了一部分袖子。}
# en: Hold the water line
opt.right.label [efca5e] = 守住水线
# en: {You stand in the shallows holding a curtain of lake water for an hour. Nothing gets past you. Nobody notices, which is the point.|Your arms ache from keeping the water up. It's the least glamorous job on the shore and the one the lecturer checks first.|You hold the water line through the worst of it. When the dry reeds flare, your curtain is the one that holds.}
opt.right.say.1 [20cdcb] = {你站在浅水里撑着一道湖水帘幕，撑了一个钟头。什么都没漏过去。没人注意到，这正是要点。|手臂撑水撑得发酸。这是岸上最不光彩的差事，却是讲师头一个检查的。|你在最凶险的时候撑住了水线。干芦苇蹿起火来时，撑住的正是你那道水帘。}

@event evo_drowned_flame
# en: Fire Under Water
title [29fc18] = 水下之火
# en: {Original work in Advanced Evocation, a fire that burns underwater. Every student gets a tank. Most tanks get a new pane every week.|Your tank is waiting, with a fresh crack along one pane.|The tank again. You talk to the water now, and to the fire, separately.} {Someone's tank has boiled dry and they're staring at it.|A flame at the next bench burns green beneath the water, quite calm.|The lecturer is standing well back today.}
text [b9657b] = {高等塑能术的原创作业：一团在水下燃烧的火。每人一只水箱。大多数水箱每周都要换块新玻璃。|你的水箱在等你，一块玻璃上新添了一道裂纹。|又是水箱。如今你会分别跟水和火说话。} {有人的水箱烧干了，他们正盯着它发呆。|邻桌一团火在水底燃着绿光，十分平静。|讲师今天站得远远的。}
# en: A glass tank of water on a scorched bench, a small blue flame burning steadily at the bottom of it.
scene [c9026b] = 一张烧焦的长桌上放着一只玻璃水箱，一小团蓝色火焰在箱底稳稳燃烧。
# en: Light it at the bottom
opt.left.label [a339ad] = 在箱底点燃它
# en: {A small blue flame takes hold under the water and stays. The bubbles go up in a thin silver line.|It catches, gutters, and settles. The water around it doesn't even warm. You don't know how you did it.|You light it while the lecturer stands well back. It burns, small and stubborn, and the lecturer comes a step closer.}
opt.left.say.1 [1987da] = {一小团蓝火在水下点着了，并且留了下来。气泡排成一道细细的银线往上冒。|它点着了，摇晃了一下，安顿下来。周围的水甚至没变暖。你也不知道自己是怎么做到的。|你点火时讲师站得远远的。它烧着了，小小的，很倔，讲师往前走了一步。}
# en: {The water boils in a heartbeat and the pane splits. You wear the steam on your face for the rest of the day.|The flame goes up instead of in. The tank cracks, and your sleeve is wet and scorched at once.|You learn why the lecturer is standing back. The pane goes, and so does your eyebrow.}
opt.left.say.2 [b4a824] = {水一瞬间就沸了，玻璃裂开。一整天你脸上都带着那股蒸汽。|火没往里钻，反往上蹿。水箱裂了，你的袖子同时又湿又焦。|你明白了讲师为什么站得那么远。玻璃碎了，你的一边眉毛也没了。}
# en: Wrap it in a bubble first
opt.right.label [69bcca] = 先裹一个气泡
# en: {You hold a skin of air around the flame and sink them both. It's half a cheat, and the lecturer says so. It burns all hour.|Your flame sits in a bubble at the bottom like a moth in a jar. Not the assignment, but not nothing.|You wrap it in a bubble, as you always do now. The lecturer says it's time to try without, and doesn't make you.}
opt.right.say.1 [495623] = {你用一层空气包住火，把它们一起沉下去。这算半个作弊，讲师也这么说。但它烧了一整节课。|你的火待在箱底的气泡里，像罐子里的飞蛾。不是作业要求的，但也不是什么都没有。|你像现在每次那样，给它裹上气泡。讲师说是时候试试不用了，但没有逼你。}

@event astro_sealed_forecast
# en: Tomorrow's Weather
title [fdb53c] = 明日天气
# en: {Foresight at Astromancy II. Write down tomorrow's weather to the hour, seal it, pin it to the board. The lecturer opens the envelopes a day later, in public.|The envelopes come out again.|You've written so many forecasts you dream in drizzle.} {Outside the dome the sky is giving nothing away.|Last week's best forecast just said "Wet", and was right.|{season == "winter": Frost on the dome, and snow somewhere in the future.|Clouds over the lake, moving with intent.}}
text [7b1548] = {星象学 II 的预见课。写下明天每个时辰的天气，封好，钉到板上。讲师第二天会当众拆信。|信封又拿出来了。|你写过太多预报，连做梦都在下毛毛雨。} {穹顶外的天空什么都不肯透露。|上周最好的预报只写了一个“湿”字，而且对了。|{season == "winter": 穹顶上结了霜，未来某处有雪。|湖上的云正带着目的移动。}}
# en: A row of sealed envelopes pinned to a corkboard in the observatory, each labelled with a student's name and tomorrow's date.
scene [63cf64] = 观星台的软木板上钉着一排封好的信封，每只都写着学生的名字和明天的日期。
# en: Commit to the hour
opt.left.label [1bcf44] = 精确到时辰
# en: {"Rain at the third bell, stopping at the fourth." It does. The lecturer reads it out twice.|You forecast a fog to the hour. When the envelope is opened, the fog is pressing on the dome.|You write "Sleet at the second bell, from the lake." It comes off the lake at the second bell. The lecturer stops reading the others.}
opt.left.say.1 [39d2c0] = {“三更钟时下雨，四更钟停。”果然如此。讲师念了两遍。|你预报了一场准点的雾。信封拆开时，雾正贴在穹顶上。|你写下“二更钟，湖上来雨夹雪。”二更钟时，雨夹雪果然从湖上来了。讲师不再念别人的了。}
# en: {"Clear by noon." It rains till evening. Your envelope is read out to great enjoyment.|You predicted wind. Tomorrow turns out so still that a feather on the sill doesn't move.|You forecast with great confidence. Tomorrow is the opposite of everything you wrote, in order.}
opt.left.say.2 [fda6b5] = {“午前转晴。”雨一直下到傍晚。你的信封被念出来，大家听得很开心。|你预报有风。结果第二天静得连窗台上的羽毛都没动一下。|你信心满满地写下预报。第二天的天气和你写的每一条都相反，而且顺序一致。}
# en: Hedge, and learn from it
opt.right.label [53eefc] = 留有余地，边看边学
# en: {"Some weather, at some point." The lecturer reads it out flatly and moves on. But you spent the hour watching how the good forecasters work.|You write a careful forecast with three possibilities. It's right, technically. The lecturer calls it "an umbrella of a prophecy".|You hedge, and read the others' envelopes after. You can tell the good ones by how short they are.}
opt.right.say.1 [5376c0] = {“某个时候会有某种天气。”讲师面无表情地念完，继续下一个。但这一节课你都在看高手们怎么做。|你写了一份周全的预报，列了三种可能。严格说它是对的。讲师称之为“一把伞似的预言”。|你写得模棱两可，之后读了别人的信封。好的预报一看就知道，因为它们都很短。}

@event astro_stubborn_telescope
# en: The Stubborn Telescope
title [2959bb] = 倔强的望远镜
# en: {Astromancy II needs exact positions, and that means a night on the great telescope. At the morning lecture your name goes up on tonight's rota. The great telescope, everyone warns you, points wherever it likes.|Your name is on tonight's telescope rota again. The lecturer warns you it is already pointing at something else.|Your night on the telescope again. The lecturer only raises an eyebrow at you as the rota goes up.} {This week it wants the moon.|This week it's fixed on the lake, which is not in the sky.|This week it keeps drifting east, slowly, like a sigh.}
text [278ba4] = {星象学 II 需要精确的星位，这就得在大望远镜前熬一夜。早课上，你的名字被排进了今晚的轮值表。大家都提醒你：大望远镜爱指哪儿就指哪儿。|今晚的望远镜轮值表上又有你。讲师提醒你，它已经指着别处了。|又轮到你守望远镜。轮值表贴出来时，讲师只是冲你挑了挑眉。} {这周它想看月亮。|这周它盯着湖面，可湖不在天上。|这周它一直慢慢往东偏，像一声叹息。}
# en: A student tugging at a huge brass telescope in a dome, while it points stubbornly at a different patch of sky.
scene [6f250f] = 穹顶下，一名学生拽着一架巨大的黄铜望远镜，它却固执地指着另一片天空。
# en: Argue it round
opt.left.label [dba882] = 把它劝回来
# en: {You coax it, inch by inch, and it settles on your star with a creak like a shrug.|You find the right thing to say to an old brass instrument. It points where you ask. You write the position fast.|You coax it off its eastward drift with a gentle hand and a sharp word. It sighs back to your star.}
opt.left.say.1 [1f875f] = {你一寸一寸地哄它，它终于停在你的星上，嘎吱一声，像是耸了耸肩。|你找到了对一件老黄铜仪器该说的话。它指向你要的地方。你飞快地记下星位。|你温柔地推、严厉地说，把它从往东漂的劲头里哄了回来。它叹着气回到了你的星上。}
# en: {It spends the night pointing where it likes. So do you, in the end, cold and annoyed.|You lean on it. It leans back. You go to bed at the fourth bell with nothing written down.|It drifts east all night, slowly, and takes you with it. You write down a very good position for the wrong star.}
opt.left.say.2 [47a320] = {它整晚都指着它想指的地方。最后你也只好陪着，又冷又恼。|你靠在它身上使劲，它也靠回来。四更钟你上床时，本子上一个字都没有。|它整晚都在慢慢往东漂，把你也带走了。你为一颗错的星记下了一个非常精确的位置。}
# en: Work it out from tables
opt.right.label [0fbd24] = 用星表推算
# en: {You leave the telescope to its moods and work the positions out by candlelight from the old tables. It takes until dawn.|Pages of sums by candle. The telescope watches over your shoulder, pointedly.|You use the tables and let the telescope drift where it likes. Your positions are good, and you're in bed by midnight.}
opt.right.say.1 [53ea77] = {你随望远镜闹脾气去，借着烛光用旧星表把星位算出来。一直算到天亮。|一页又一页的烛下演算。望远镜在你肩后盯着，意味深长。|你用星表，任望远镜漂去它想去的地方。星位算得不错，午夜前你就上床了。}

@event astro_long_watch
# en: Keeping the Light
title [72610b] = 守住星光
# en: {Advanced Starlight. At the morning lecture you're given tonight's task. Hold one star's light in a lantern through a whole night on the roof. It will want to go home before dawn. Your job is to keep it.|The night watch on the roof comes round again. After the morning lecture you collect a lantern and a blanket.|Your lantern, your star, your corner of the roof, booked for tonight.} {The star you've drawn is pale and blue.|The star you've drawn is small and stubborn.|The star you've drawn is very old and very faint.} {season == "winter": There will be frost on the slates.|The night will be warm and full of moths.}
text [903ab3] = {高等星光课。早课上，你领到了今晚的任务。把一颗星的光装进灯笼，在屋顶守上一整夜。天亮前它会想回家，你的任务是留住它。|又轮到屋顶守夜了。早课后，你领了一盏灯笼和一条毯子。|你的灯笼，你的星，你在屋顶的那个角落，今晚都订好了。} {你抽到的星又淡又蓝。|你抽到的星又小又倔。|你抽到的星非常古老，非常微弱。} {season == "winter": 石板瓦上会结霜。|今夜会很温暖，满是飞蛾。}
# en: A student on the observatory roof before dawn, a glass lantern in their lap holding a single cold point of starlight.
scene [efcd22] = 天亮前的观星台屋顶上，一名学生膝上放着一盏玻璃灯笼，里面装着一点冷冷的星光。
# en: Keep it all night
opt.left.label [828910] = 守它一整夜
# en: {At dawn your star is still in the lantern, blinking at the sun it was never meant to meet. You are blinking too.|You keep it till the lecturer comes up at sunrise. Your eyes are full of sand and your lantern is full of light.|Your old faint star almost goes out at the fourth bell. You talk to it until dawn, and it stays.}
opt.left.say.1 [8f3c73] = {天亮时你的星还在灯笼里，对着它本不该遇见的太阳眨眼。你也在眨眼。|你一直守到讲师日出时上来。你眼里全是沙，灯笼里全是光。|你那颗古老而微弱的星在四更钟几乎熄灭。你跟它说话说到天亮，它留下了。}
# en: Let it go at midnight
opt.right.label [d7678c] = 午夜放它走
# en: {You open the lantern and the light goes up like a kite let loose. You watch it all the way home and then go to bed.|You let it go early. The lecturer's note just says "Released at midnight." You suspect it's not a compliment.|You let the old star go at midnight. It goes slowly, as if it isn't sure of the way. You watch it until you can't.}
opt.right.say.1 [c4bdd3] = {你打开灯笼，光像脱了线的风筝一样升上去。你一路目送它回家，然后去睡觉。|你早早放了它。讲师的记录上只写着“午夜放归”。你怀疑这不是夸奖。|你在午夜放走了那颗老星。它走得很慢，好像不太认得路。你一直看到看不见为止。}
# en: Feed it your own starlight
opt.up.label [07c1bd] = 喂它你的星光
# en: {You pour a little of your own starlight into the lantern. The star brightens as if it had been lonely.|Your light and the star's together are enough to read by. You read until dawn.|You give the old star some of your light. It burns brighter than it has in a long time, and you feel it go out of you.}
opt.up.say.1 [89444f] = {你往灯笼里倒了一点自己的星光。那颗星亮了起来，好像它一直很寂寞。|你的光和星的光合在一起，足够看书了。你一直读到天亮。|你把自己的光分了一些给那颗老星。它烧得比很久以来都亮，你感觉到那份光从你身上流走了。}

@event astro_two_futures
# en: Both Futures
title [c2e1aa] = 两种未来
# en: {Advanced Foresight. The lecturer balances a coin on its edge. Read both futures at once, the one where it falls heads and the one where it falls tails, and hold them both.|The coin on its edge again. You know how it feels to be two places at once now.|The coin. People come out of this lesson pressing their temples.} {Someone in the front row says "heads" in two voices.|The lecturer is drinking tea and looking at nobody.|The candles burn straight up, very still.}
text [8cb25c] = {高等预见课。讲师把一枚硬币立在边缘上。同时读出两种未来，正面落地的那个和反面落地的那个，并把两者都握住。|又是立着的硬币。如今你知道同时身处两地是什么感觉了。|硬币。走出这节课的人都按着太阳穴。} {前排有人用两个声音说“正面”。|讲师在喝茶，谁也不看。|烛火笔直向上，一动不动。}
# en: A coin balanced on edge on a dark table in the observatory, with two faint ghostly outcomes hovering above it.
scene [137628] = 观星台一张深色桌上，一枚硬币立在边缘，上方悬浮着两个淡淡的、幽灵似的结果。
# en: Hold both to the end
opt.left.label [acd6d2] = 两者握到最后
# en: {For a long moment you live both futures, side by side, and neither is frightening. Then the coin falls, and one of them goes out.|You hold both until the lecturer flicks the coin. One future folds away, neat as a letter.|You hold both in the still candlelight until the lecturer stops the coin with a finger. Both futures are still there. "Interesting," the lecturer says.}
opt.left.say.1 [7dbfc6] = {有那么长长的一刻，你并肩活在两种未来里，哪一种都不可怕。然后硬币倒下，其中一种熄灭了。|你一直握着两者，直到讲师弹倒硬币。一种未来折了起来，整齐得像一封信。|你在一动不动的烛光里握住两者，直到讲师用一根手指按住硬币。两种未来都还在。“有意思，”讲师说。}
# en: {The futures tangle and you get a headache that lasts till supper. For an hour you keep reaching for the wrong door handle.|You lose track of which future is which, and of which way is down. The lecturer sits you by an open window.|You hold both too long. For the rest of the day you hear things a moment before they happen, and you hate it.}
opt.left.say.2 [91f883] = {两种未来缠在一起，你头疼到晚饭。之后一个钟头你总是去拧错的门把手。|你分不清哪个未来是哪个了，也分不清哪边是下。讲师让你坐到开着的窗边。|你握得太久了。这一整天你都比别人早一刻听到事情发生，你讨厌这种感觉。}
# en: Read one, then the other
opt.right.label [e61653] = 先读一个，再读另一个
# en: {You read heads, then tails, carefully, one after the other. It's not the exercise, but you get both right.|One future at a time. Slower, safer, and the lecturer says you'll get there.|One future, then the other, and you know both now before you read them. The lecturer says that's the start of holding them.}
opt.right.say.1 [95f2f8] = {你先读正面，再读反面，一个接一个，小心翼翼。这不是练习的要求，但两个你都读对了。|一次一个未来。更慢，更稳，讲师说你会做到的。|一个未来，然后是另一个，现在你还没读就知道两个了。讲师说这是握住它们的开始。}

@event alch_unlabelled_vial
# en: The Unlabelled Vial
title [ec7cd4] = 没有标签的药瓶
# en: {Alchemy II hands out an unlabelled vial each, and an hour to say what's in it. Paper strips, a candle, a nose and a notebook are allowed.|Another unlabelled vial. The lecturer enjoys these.|The vial is waiting on your bench. You've started recognising the corks.} {Yours is perfectly clear and smells faintly of pears.|Yours is cloudy and keeps settling into layers.|Yours is warm to the touch.} {The ventilation charm is wheezing again.|The lab is quiet except for scratching quills.|The lecturer is humming, which means the vials are harder this week.}
text [8be139] = {炼金 II 发给每人一只没有标签的药瓶，一个钟头内说出里面是什么。试纸、蜡烛、鼻子和笔记本都可以用。|又是没标签的药瓶。讲师很享受这个。|药瓶在你桌上等着。你已经开始认得那些软木塞了。} {你的这瓶清澈透明，隐约有股梨香。|你的这瓶浑浊，总是沉淀分层。|你的这瓶摸上去是温的。} {通风咒又在喘了。|实验室里很安静，只有羽毛笔沙沙作响。|讲师在哼歌，这说明这周的瓶子更难了。}
# en: A vial of clear liquid on a lab bench beside a strip of paper turning slowly purple, a student squinting at both.
scene [3b7b2e] = 实验台上放着一瓶透明液体，旁边一条试纸正慢慢变紫，一名学生眯着眼看着两者。
# en: Test it the long way
opt.left.label [2f891a] = 老老实实逐项测
# en: {Strip, flame, cold, filter. By the end of the hour you've a name and three reasons for it.|Every test, in order, written up neatly. Your notes are dull and your answer is right.|The warm one takes the whole hour, test by test. It's something you've never met, and you name it anyway, correctly.}
opt.left.say.1 [b95931] = {试纸、火焰、冷却、过滤。一个钟头结束时，你有了一个名字和三条理由。|每一项测试，按部就班，写得工工整整。你的笔记很无聊，答案是对的。|那瓶温热的花了整整一个钟头，一项一项地测。是你从没遇到过的东西，但你还是叫出了它的名字，而且叫对了。}
# en: Trust your nose
opt.right.label [c495ff] = 相信你的鼻子
# en: {One sniff and you know it. You write the name and use the spare hour to check yourself.|You tip the vial under your nose and the answer arrives before the smell does. The lecturer raises an eyebrow and a tick.|It's warm, and that tells you most of it. You sniff to confirm. The lecturer stops humming.}
opt.right.say.1 [73827a] = {一闻你就知道了。你写下名字，用多出来的一个钟头检查自己。|你把瓶子凑到鼻子下，答案比气味先到。讲师挑了挑眉，打了个勾。|它是温的，这就说明了大半。你闻了一下确认。讲师不哼歌了。}
# en: {One sniff and your eyes stream for the rest of the morning. You guessed wrong, too.|It's not what you thought, and it is very much up your nose. You spend the hour at the window.|You sniff the warm one. It sniffs back, in a way, and you spend the hour with a damp cloth on your face.}
opt.right.say.2 [82aa3d] = {一闻之下，你整个上午都在流眼泪。而且你还猜错了。|它不是你以为的东西，而且结结实实冲进了你的鼻子。这一节课你都待在窗边。|你闻了闻那瓶温热的。某种意义上它也闻了闻你，这一节课你都捂着一块湿布。}

@event alch_cracked_tray
# en: The Cracked Tray
title [a94d69] = 一盘裂物
# en: {Mend at Alchemy II. Sister Amaranth sets out a tray of cracked things, cup, mirror and bone. "Mend those," she says, "and then we'll see about people."|The tray again. Sister Amaranth has found new things to crack.|Sister Amaranth puts the tray down and nods at it. You know the drill.} {A second-year is waiting on a cot with a sprained wrist from broom practice.|A third-year with a scalded hand from Evocation is waiting.|A first-year is in with a split lip and a long story about a door.}
text [7de022] = {炼金 II 的愈合课。阿玛兰斯修女摆出一盘裂开的东西：杯子、镜子、骨头。“先把这些补好，”她说，“然后再说人。”|又是这盘东西。阿玛兰斯修女找到了新的可以弄裂的东西。|阿玛兰斯修女放下托盘，朝它点点头。你知道该怎么做。} {一个二年级生坐在病床上等着，手腕是练飞帚时扭的。|一个在塑能课上烫伤手的三年级生在等着。|一个一年级生嘴唇裂了，正讲着一个关于门的长故事。}
# en: A tray in the infirmary laid with a cracked teacup, a cracked hand mirror and a cracked bone from a teaching skeleton, a student's hands hovering over them.
scene [a85abf] = 医务室里一只托盘，放着一只裂开的茶杯、一面裂开的手镜和一根教学骨架上裂开的骨头，一名学生的双手悬在它们上方。
# en: Mend the tray, perfectly
opt.left.label [9eeb5c] = 把托盘补得完美
# en: {The cracks close like seams being sewn shut. Sister Amaranth runs a thumbnail along the cup and finds nothing.|Cup, mirror, bone, whole. Sister Amaranth says "Fine," which is her highest word.|You mend the tray in half the time and Sister Amaranth sends you to the first-year with the split lip. It mends cleanly.}
opt.left.say.1 [846031] = {裂缝像被缝上的接缝一样合拢。阿玛兰斯修女用拇指甲沿杯沿划过去，什么也没摸到。|杯子、镜子、骨头，全都完好。阿玛兰斯修女说“还行”，这是她的最高评价。|你只用一半的时间就补好了托盘，阿玛兰斯修女派你去给那个嘴唇裂开的一年级生看。缝得很干净。}
# en: {The cup mends with a ridge in it, the mirror with a ripple. Sister Amaranth sets them on the shelf of shame.|You mend the bone a little crooked. Sister Amaranth says that's how you learn and puts it back in the skeleton anyway.|The mirror mends with your face in it, slightly wrong. Sister Amaranth turns it to the wall.}
opt.left.say.2 [0cb5fe] = {杯子补好了，却留了一道棱；镜子补好了，却起了一道波纹。阿玛兰斯修女把它们放上了耻辱架。|你把骨头补得有点歪。阿玛兰斯修女说这就是学习，还是把它装回了骨架。|镜子补好了，里面却留着你的脸，还有点走样。阿玛兰斯修女把它翻过去对着墙。}
# en: Mend the patient instead
opt.right.label [c58841] = 改去治病人
# en: {You skip the tray and take the patient, with Sister Amaranth's hand on your shoulder. It goes slowly. It works.|Sister Amaranth lets you try on the patient while she watches. You're shaky and slow, and you'll never mend a cup the same way again.|You mend the first-year's lip and hear the whole story about the door. It wasn't a door. You keep that to yourself.}
opt.right.say.1 [c520ad] = {你跳过托盘，接手病人，阿玛兰斯修女的手搭在你肩上。进展很慢，但成了。|阿玛兰斯修女看着你在病人身上试。你手抖，动作慢，而且从此再也不会用原来的方式补杯子了。|你给那个一年级生缝好了嘴唇，听了关于那扇门的全部故事。根本不是门。你没说出去。}

@event alch_lake_fever
# en: Lake Fever Season
title [5e2ca1] = 湖热季
# en: {Advanced Alchemy treats real patients. The infirmary has Lake Fever cases, from swimming where they shouldn't. Sister Amaranth wants the fever drawn out, not just cooled.|Lake Fever again. Students never learn, Sister Amaranth says, and neither do lakes.|Fever duty. Sister Amaranth hands you a list without looking up.} {Your patient says they only went in up to the knees.|Your patient is a prefect, very embarrassed.|Your patient insists they were pushed.}
text [d87cd6] = {高等炼金要治真正的病人。医务室里有湖热病例，都是在不该游泳的地方游了泳。阿玛兰斯修女要你把热病拔出来，而不只是降温。|又是湖热。修女说，学生从不长记性，湖也不长。|退热值班。阿玛兰斯修女头也不抬地递给你一张名单。} {你的病人说他们只下水到膝盖。|你的病人是一位级长，非常难为情。|你的病人坚称是被人推下去的。}
# en: A row of infirmary cots, students under blankets looking flushed and sorry for themselves, an advanced student drawing a faint grey haze out of one patient's brow.
scene [4db536] = 一排医务室病床，学生们裹着毯子，满脸通红，可怜兮兮；一名高年级生正从一位病人额头上抽出一缕淡淡的灰雾。
# en: Draw the fever out by hand
opt.left.label [cf9f68] = 亲手把热拔出来
# en: {The fever comes out like a grey thread pulled from wool. Your patient sleeps. You'd like to.|You draw it out slowly and the flush leaves their face. Sister Amaranth checks your work and doesn't check twice.|You draw out the fever and the story with it. They were pushed. Sister Amaranth writes down the name.}
opt.left.say.1 [5d5e1c] = {热病像从羊毛里抽出的一根灰线，被你拉了出来。病人睡着了。你也很想睡。|你慢慢把它抽出来，潮红从他们脸上退去。阿玛兰斯修女检查了你的活儿，没有检查第二遍。|你把热病连同那个故事一起拔了出来。对方确实是被推下去的。阿玛兰斯修女记下了那个名字。}
# en: {You draw out half of it and the half you drew comes with you. You spend the evening shivering in the next cot.|The cure has to come from somewhere. You wake up two hours later on the floor, with a blanket on you.|The fever comes out angry and goes into you. You spend the night in the next cot, insisting you weren't pushed.}
opt.left.say.2 [520af0] = {你只拔出了一半，而拔出来的那一半跟上了你。整个晚上你都在隔壁病床上发抖。|治愈总得从某处来。两个钟头后你在地板上醒来，身上盖着一条毯子。|热病带着怒气出来，钻进了你身上。你在隔壁病床上过了一夜，一个劲儿地说自己不是被推下去的。}
# en: Brew the slow tonic
opt.right.label [af7952] = 熬慢效补剂
# en: {Three hours of stirring willow bark and lake moss. The tonic works by morning, which is slower and safer.|You brew the old remedy by the book. Sister Amaranth tastes it, grimaces, and approves.|You brew the tonic without the book now. Sister Amaranth tastes it and doesn't grimace, which worries you more.}
opt.right.say.1 [ed12ab] = {三个钟头搅着柳树皮和湖苔。补剂到早上才见效，慢一些，也稳一些。|你照书熬了老方子。阿玛兰斯修女尝了一口，皱了皱脸，点头认可。|现在你不看书也能熬这补剂了。阿玛兰斯修女尝了一口，没皱脸，这反倒让你更担心了。}
# en: Purify it in one pass
opt.up.label [f808f7] = 一次净化干净
# en: {Your spell pulls the fever clean in a single pass. It leaves you yawning.|One pass of Purify and the patient sits up asking for soup. The tiredness lands on you an hour later.|You purify it in one pass, and your patient sits up and says who pushed them. You're asleep before Sister Amaranth asks.}
opt.up.say.1 [83434a] = {你的咒语一遍就把热病拔得干干净净。它让你直打哈欠。|一遍净化，病人就坐起来要汤喝。一个钟头后，疲倦落到了你身上。|你一遍就净化干净了，病人坐起来说出了是谁推的。阿玛兰斯修女还没来得及问，你已经睡着了。}

@event alch_third_floor_still
# en: The Still Cracks
title [7ecae5] = 蒸馏器裂了
# en: {Advanced Alchemy distils essences that would rather be gas. The ventilation charm gave up on the third floor years ago. Today your still cracks.|Distilling day, and a hiss from your still that you know.|Your still has cracked again. You're getting fast at noticing.} {The vapour is green and smells of mint.|The vapour is pale and smells of nothing, which is worse.|The vapour is curling toward the next bench.}
text [fbd2ac] = {高等炼金要蒸馏那些宁愿当气体的精华。三楼的通风咒多年前就放弃了。今天你的蒸馏器裂了。|蒸馏日，你的蒸馏器又发出那种你熟悉的嘶嘶声。|你的蒸馏器又裂了。你发现得越来越快了。} {蒸汽是绿的，有薄荷味。|蒸汽颜色很淡，什么味道都没有，这更糟。|蒸汽正卷向隔壁的实验台。}
# en: A copper still on a long bench, hissing from a fresh crack, a thin green vapour creeping across the laboratory floor.
scene [e5be1b] = 长实验台上一只铜蒸馏器从新裂口里嘶嘶作响，一缕淡绿色的蒸汽正爬过实验室的地板。
# en: Mend the crack, still hot
opt.left.label [127d5d] = 趁热把裂缝补上
# en: {You close the copper under your palms while it's still singing. The hiss stops. The class breathes out.|The crack seals with a sound like a sigh, and the batch is saved. The lecturer opens a window, for form's sake.|You seal it before the vapour reaches the next bench. Its owner never knows how close it came.}
opt.left.say.1 [a9fb6d] = {铜还在嗡鸣，你就用掌心把它合上了。嘶声停了，全班松了口气。|裂缝合拢，发出一声叹息般的轻响，这一批保住了。讲师还是开了扇窗，走个形式。|你在蒸汽飘到隔壁台子之前封好了它。台子的主人永远不知道刚才有多悬。}
# en: {The crack closes, then reopens with a pop. You breathe in a mouthful and spend the afternoon seeing double.|You burn your fingertips on the copper and the vapour gets out anyway. The lab is cleared for an hour.|The vapour reaches the next bench before you do. Two of you spend the afternoon seeing double.}
opt.left.say.2 [a9cec7] = {裂缝合上了，又“噗”地一声裂开。你吸进一大口，整个下午看东西都是重影。|你的指尖被铜烫伤，蒸汽还是跑了出来。实验室清场一个钟头。|蒸汽比你先到了隔壁的台子。你们两个整个下午看东西都是重影。}
# en: Shout, and clear the bench
opt.right.label [17c853] = 大喊一声，清空台面
# en: {You call the warning and clear the bench. The batch is lost, nobody is hurt, and you start again next week.|Everyone is out in the corridor in a minute flat. The lecturer goes back in, a scarf over the mouth, and comes out carrying your ruined batch.|You clear the bench and the one next to it. The lecturer notes that you thought of the neighbours, and the batch is still lost.}
opt.right.say.1 [ac5419] = {你喊出警告，清空了台面。这一批毁了，没人受伤，你下周重来。|一分钟内所有人都到了走廊上。讲师用围巾捂着口鼻回去，把你那批报废的东西端了出来。|你清空了自己的台子，也清空了隔壁的。讲师注意到你考虑到了邻座，可这一批还是毁了。}

@event illu_walking_double
# en: The Walking Double
title [188b9c] = 会走的分身
# en: {Mirror at Illusion II. Make a double of yourself and walk it across the room. "Standing doubles are furniture," says Professor Vey. "Make it walk."|Doubles day. Vey watches feet, not faces.|Your double's walk is improving. It has your slouch now.} {The floor has been dusted with chalk, to show footprints.|Someone's double is walking backwards.|Vey is sitting in the front row, which is unsettling.}
text [6e95b9] = {幻术 II 的镜像课。给自己造一个分身，让它走过教室。“站着的分身是家具，”维伊教授说，“让它走。”|分身日。维伊看脚，不看脸。|你的分身走得越来越好了。它现在连你的驼背都学会了。} {地上撒了粉笔灰，好显出脚印。|有人的分身在倒着走。|维伊坐在第一排，这让人心里发毛。}
# en: Two identical students walking side by side across a lecture hall, one of them leaving no footprints in the chalk dust.
scene [45f81a] = 两个一模一样的学生并肩走过讲堂，其中一个在粉笔灰上没留下脚印。
# en: Walk it right across
opt.left.label [8d74d0] = 让它走完全程
# en: {Your double crosses the room at your pace and even scuffs the chalk. Vey watches its feet the whole way and says nothing, which is high praise.|It walks, it turns, it nearly sits down. Vey says, "Better."|Your double slouches across the room, Vey in the front row watching every step. "That's you," Vey says. It isn't a compliment, quite.}
opt.left.say.1 [836f34] = {你的分身按你的步子穿过教室，甚至蹭花了粉笔灰。维伊一路盯着它的脚，什么也没说，这是很高的赞扬。|它走，它转身，它差点坐下。维伊说：“好些了。”|你的分身弓着背穿过教室，维伊坐在第一排盯着每一步。“那就是你，”维伊说。这不全是夸奖。}
# en: {Halfway across, your double's legs forget to move and it glides. Vey says it's a ghost, not a person, and moves on.|Your double walks into the wall and keeps walking. The class watches it vanish into the plaster.|Your double sees Vey in the front row and freezes, exactly as you would. It's very lifelike, and it doesn't walk.}
opt.left.say.2 [f9609c] = {走到一半，分身的腿忘了动，开始飘。维伊说那是鬼，不是人，然后走开了。|你的分身撞上墙，还在继续走。全班看着它消失在灰泥里。|你的分身看见维伊坐在第一排就僵住了，跟你一模一样。非常逼真，可它就是不走。}
# en: Keep it still and perfect
opt.right.label [7cb3fb] = 让它站着，完美无缺
# en: {Your double stands at your elbow, perfect to the last button. It doesn't move. Vey calls it a very good wardrobe.|You make it flawless and keep it standing. Vey taps its nose, and frowns when it holds.|Your double stands perfectly still in front of Vey, slouch and all. Vey reaches out and adjusts its collar, which holds.}
opt.right.say.1 [c74e86] = {你的分身站在你手肘边，连最后一颗纽扣都完美。它不动。维伊称它是一件很好的衣橱。|你把它做得天衣无缝，然后让它站着。维伊敲了敲它的鼻子，发现敲得到，皱起了眉。|你的分身一动不动地站在维伊面前，连驼背都一样。维伊伸手理了理它的领子，领子还真在。}

@event illu_good_news
# en: Good News, Read Aloud
title [0d109c] = 当众念好消息
# en: {Glamour at Illusion II, and today it's the voice. Vey hands you a dull notice and asks you to read it so the class hears good news.|Another notice from Vey's drawer of very dull notices.|Vey has saved the dullest notice for you.} {Today's is about the drains.|Today's is about a change to the laundry rota.|Today's is a list of overdue library books, in full.}
text [f297c7] = {幻术 II 的魅影课，今天练的是声音。维伊递给你一份枯燥的通知，要你念得让全班听成好消息。|又是一份来自维伊那抽屉超级枯燥通知的通知。|维伊把最枯燥的那份留给了你。} {今天这份讲的是排水沟。|今天这份讲的是洗衣轮值表的调整。|今天这份是图书馆逾期书目，全文。}
# en: A student standing at a lectern reading from a dull notice while the listening class smiles as though hearing wonderful news.
scene [74b6a2] = 一名学生站在讲台前念着一份枯燥的通知，台下的同学们却笑容满面，像在听天大的好消息。
# en: Glamour every word
opt.left.label [3eefc7] = 字字施魅影
# en: {By the second line the room is beaming. Someone claps. Vey waits for the clapping to stop and asks what the notice said. Nobody knows.|You read it warm and low, and the class leans in as if you were reading their letters from home.|You read out the overdue books like a list of prize-winners. Three students go to the library that afternoon.}
opt.left.say.1 [af6971] = {念到第二行，满屋子都笑开了。有人鼓掌。维伊等掌声停了，问通知说了什么。没人知道。|你念得温暖而低沉，全班都探过身来，好像你在念他们的家书。|你把逾期的书单念得像获奖名单。那天下午有三个学生去了图书馆。}
# en: {Your glamour slips on a long word and the room hears exactly what it is, a notice. Someone yawns on purpose.|You overdo it. The class looks alarmed, as if the notice were about to propose.|The glamour holds for twenty titles and drops on the twenty-first. The class hears the rest exactly as they are.}
opt.left.say.2 [4f5ba7] = {魅影在一个长词上滑脱，全屋听到的正是它本来的样子：一份通知。有人故意打了个哈欠。|你用力过猛。全班一脸惊恐，好像这份通知要求婚了。|魅影撑过了二十个书名，在第二十一个上掉了下来。剩下的全班听到的都是原样。}
# en: Read it plain, watch others
opt.right.label [c74a90] = 照念，看别人
# en: {You read it straight and sit down. Then you watch the others, and notice the best of them barely change their voices at all.|Plain reading, polite applause. You spend the hour writing down where the good ones breathe.|You read the list plain. It takes a long time. You learn more watching Vey's face than you would have by trying.}
opt.right.say.1 [7cc167] = {你照原样念完坐下。然后你看别人念，发现最好的那几个几乎没怎么改变嗓音。|平平地念，礼貌的掌声。这一节课你都在记高手们在哪里换气。|你平平地念完那张清单。念了很久。看维伊的表情，你学到的比自己试还多。}
# en: Glamour the notice itself
opt.up.label [286fbe] = 给告示本身施魅影
# en: {You don't touch your voice; you glamour the paper. Every student who reads it over your shoulder sees good news in their own hand. Vey applauds, twice, slowly.|You glamour the ink so it shimmers like a wedding invitation. The class fights over the notice afterwards. It is still, underneath, a very dull notice.|You glamour the list into an honours roll. Half the class goes to look for their names, and finds their overdue books.}
opt.up.say.1 [577a68] = {你不动嗓子，而是给纸施魅影。每个从你肩后看过去的学生，都用自己的笔迹读到了好消息。维伊鼓了两下掌，很慢。|你给墨水施魅影，让它像婚礼请柬一样闪闪发光。课后全班抢那张告示。说到底，它还是一份非常无聊的通知。|你给那张清单施魅影，让它变成一份荣誉榜。半个班都跑去找自己的名字，结果找到了自己的逾期书。}

@event illu_false_room
# en: The Room That Isn't
title [04316d] = 不存在的房间
# en: {Advanced Illusion asks for a double of a whole room. Hang it over the real one and walk a classmate through it. Vey's rule is simple. If anyone walks into a wall, it's your fault.|The room exercise. Somebody always walks into something.|You hang your room. You've learned where the real walls are.} {Vey's volunteer today is a porter with a tray of cups.|Vey's volunteer today is Vey.|The real room has been rearranged overnight.}
text [307d9f] = {高等幻术要你造出一整个房间的分身，罩在真房间上，再让一个同学从中走过。维伊的规矩很简单。谁撞了墙，都算你的错。|房间练习。总有人会撞上点什么。|你把房间挂上去。你已经学会记住真墙在哪儿。} {维伊今天的志愿者是一位端着一托盘杯子的门房。|维伊今天的志愿者是维伊。|真房间昨夜被重新布置过了。}
# en: A student walking confidently into a room that is partly painted light, a real stone wall standing where the illusion shows an open doorway.
scene [487838] = 一名学生自信地走进一个部分由光绘成的房间，幻象里敞开的门洞处，其实立着一堵真正的石墙。
# en: Hang the whole room
opt.left.label [f08ac4] = 挂上整个房间
# en: {Your walker crosses the false room and sits down in a false chair, which you hold up for them. Vey writes for a long time.|The room holds. Nobody touches a real wall. Vey walks it twice to be sure.|You hang your room over the rearranged one and nobody notices which is which, including, briefly, Vey.}
opt.left.say.1 [3df0e0] = {走的人穿过假房间，坐上一把假椅子，你替他们撑住了它。维伊写了很久。|房间撑住了。没人碰到一堵真墙。维伊走了两遍才确认。|你把你的房间挂在重新布置过的那间上，没人分得清哪个是哪个，有那么一会儿，连维伊也分不清。}
# en: {Your walker steps through a door you painted onto solid stone. You catch them as they fall, take the edge of the stone on your own elbow, and walk them to Sister Amaranth with an apology.|Halfway across the room flickers, and the walker freezes. So do you, and you walk hip-first into a real chair.|You hang your room over where the walls were yesterday. The walker finds today's walls with their nose.}
opt.left.say.2 [1e6334] = {走的人迈进了你画在实心石头上的门。你在他们倒下时接住了，自己的手肘磕上了石棱，然后带着歉意把他们送到阿玛兰斯修女那里。|走到一半房间闪了一下，走的人僵住了。你也僵住了，胯骨一头撞上了一把真椅子。|你把房间挂在了昨天墙所在的地方。走的人用鼻子找到了今天的墙。}
# en: Chalk the real walls first
opt.right.label [26c22a] = 先用粉笔标出真墙
# en: {You hang half a room, with the real walls marked out in chalk so nobody could miss them. Vey calls it "a room with a safety rope".|Safe and visible, chalk lines everywhere. Vey sighs, and then copies down how you did the window.|You chalk the new walls first, all of them. Vey says that's the only correct answer to a rearranged room.}
opt.right.say.1 [d4e5f8] = {你只挂了半个房间，真墙都用粉笔标了出来，谁也不会错过。维伊称之为“系了安全绳的房间”。|安全，显眼，到处是粉笔线。维伊叹了口气，然后抄下了你做窗户的方法。|你先把新墙都用粉笔标了出来，一面不落。维伊说，对一间重新布置过的房间，这是唯一正确的答案。}

@event illu_peeling_layers
# en: Seeing Through
title [014ea1] = 看穿
# en: {Advanced Illusion. To make illusions you must see through them. Vey layers the hall in false rooms, one on another, and you peel them back one at a time.|Layer day. The hall looks normal. That's never a good sign.|You count the layers when you come in. You're usually wrong.} {The top layer has velvet curtains.|The top layer is a summer garden.|The top layer is the hall itself, just slightly too tidy.}
text [fa4567] = {高等幻术。要造幻象，就得先学会看穿幻象。维伊把讲堂层层罩上假房间，一层叠一层，你要一层一层揭开。|分层日。讲堂看起来很正常。这从来不是好兆头。|你一进门就数层数。你通常数错。} {最上面一层挂着天鹅绒帘子。|最上面一层是夏日花园。|最上面一层就是讲堂本身，只是整洁得有点过分。}
# en: A lecture hall in layers like peeled paper: one layer with velvet curtains, one bare stone, one darker one beneath, and a student standing at its centre.
scene [ee496c] = 一间像剥开的纸一样分层的讲堂：一层挂着天鹅绒帘子，一层是裸露的石头，下面还有更暗的一层，一名学生站在中央。
# en: Peel down to the stone
opt.left.label [12cf64] = 一直揭到石头
# en: {Seven layers, then bare stone. Vey asks how many. You say seven. She smiles and says eight, and points at herself.|You reach the stone and stay there, sure of it. Vey nods slowly. "Hold on to that," she says.|The too-tidy hall comes off last, and under it is the real hall, untidy and wonderful. Vey says you're the first today.}
opt.left.say.1 [3ff14c] = {七层，然后是裸石。维伊问几层。你说七层。她笑着说八层，指了指自己。|你揭到石头，并且停在那里，确信无疑。维伊慢慢点头。“抓住这个感觉，”她说。|太整洁的讲堂最后被揭下，底下是真正的讲堂，乱糟糟的，美极了。维伊说你是今天第一个。}
# en: {You peel one too many and the stone underneath looks false. For the rest of the day you knock on walls, with a headache behind your eyes.|After the fourth layer you stop being sure which way is up. Vey walks you to a chair, which is real.|You peel the tidy hall and find another tidy hall. And another. Vey stops you at the sixth, gently.}
opt.left.say.2 [a76a84] = {你多揭了一层，底下的石头看起来也像假的。这一整天你都在敲墙，眼睛后面隐隐作痛。|揭到第四层后，你再也不确定哪边是上。维伊把你领到一把椅子前，那把椅子是真的。|你揭开整洁的讲堂，下面还是一个整洁的讲堂。又一个。维伊在第六层时轻轻叫停了你。}
# en: Stop at the third layer
opt.right.label [b16cdd] = 揭到第三层就停
# en: {Three layers and you stop, dizzy. Vey says knowing when to stop is the other half of the skill.|You get through three and sit down. The hall still looks too tidy, and you decide not to ask.|You stop at three, and you're right to: the third was the real one. Vey says so, with some surprise.}
opt.right.say.1 [9d3b88] = {三层，你停下来，头晕目眩。维伊说，知道何时停下是这门技艺的另一半。|你揭了三层就坐下了。讲堂看起来还是太整洁，你决定不问。|你在第三层停下了，停得没错：第三层就是真的。维伊这么说了，有点意外。}

@event beast_hedge_run
# en: The Hedge Run
title [d8e2dc] = 越篱飞行
# en: {Beastcraft II puts haste on a broom, low over the hedges, as fast as you dare. Professor Brask says brooms are harder to reason with than hippogriffs, and harder to apologise to.|The hedge run. Your broom remembers last time.|Hedges. You've learned to read a broom's sulk through the handle.} {Brask is timing with a crooked hourglass.|The hedges have been trimmed, unevenly.|{season == "autumn": Leaves come up behind every broom.|{season == "spring": The hedges are full of nesting birds who object.|The ground is hard and unforgiving.}}}
text [7b76b5] = {驭兽学 II 把疾速用在飞帚上，贴着树篱低飞，能多快就多快。布拉斯克教授说，飞帚比鹰头马身有翼兽更难讲道理，也更难道歉。|越篱飞行。你的飞帚记得上一次。|树篱。你已经学会从帚柄上读出飞帚的闷气。} {布拉斯克拿着一只歪沙漏计时。|树篱修剪过了，修得高低不平。|{season == "autumn": 每把飞帚身后都扬起落叶。|{season == "spring": 树篱里满是筑巢的鸟，它们很有意见。|地面又硬又不饶人。}}}
# en: Students on brooms skimming low over a line of hedges in a field, one broom bucking as its rider leans forward.
scene [a6f163] = 学生们骑着飞帚贴着田里的一排树篱掠过，其中一把飞帚在骑手前倾时尥起了蹶子。
# en: Haste at the last hedge
opt.left.label [73bbd3] = 最后一道篱前加速
# en: {You borrow a hawk's speed for the last hedge and clear it by a hand. Brask stops the hourglass and nods.|The broom flinches, then commits. You come in fastest of the morning, with hedge in your hair.|You feel the broom's sulk through the handle and haste it anyway, kindly. It clears the last hedge and forgives you.}
opt.left.say.1 [8af82a] = {你借来鹰的速度飞越最后一道树篱，高出一掌。布拉斯克停了沙漏，点了点头。|飞帚一缩，然后豁出去了。你是这个早上最快的，头发里还挂着树篱。|你从帚柄上感觉到它在赌气，还是温和地给它加了疾速。它越过最后一道树篱，原谅了你。}
# en: {The broom bucks at the haste and you go over the hedge without it.|You're fast. The broom is faster, briefly, and then upside down. You land in a bramble.|The broom has been sulking all morning and saves it for the last hedge. You go over; it stays.}
opt.left.say.2 [96ca99] = {飞帚被疾速一惊，你独自越过了树篱，它没跟上。|你很快。飞帚短暂地比你更快，然后翻了个底朝天。你落进了荆棘丛。|飞帚赌了一上午的气，全留到了最后一道树篱。你过去了，它留下了。}
# en: Fly it clean and steady
opt.right.label [caf423] = 飞得干净平稳
# en: {No haste, just a clean low line over every hedge. Brask says it's the best boring flying she's seen all week.|You fly it slow and tidy. The broom approves. Brask is less impressed.|You fly it steady and let it sulk. Brask says the broom will remember you were patient, and so will she.}
opt.right.say.1 [27f320] = {不用疾速，每道树篱都是一条干净的低线。布拉斯克说这是她这周见过最好的无聊飞行。|你飞得又慢又整齐。飞帚很满意。布拉斯克没那么满意。|你飞得稳稳的，由它赌气。布拉斯克说飞帚会记得你有耐心，她也会。}

@event beast_owl_post
# en: Teaching the Owls
title [ba75dc] = 教猫头鹰送信
# en: {Beast-speech at Beastcraft II. The young owls must learn the post routes. Brask hands you one and says, "Explain the castle to it."|A new young owl, and the same castle to explain.|Another owl. You've got a speech now, and a map scratched on a beam.} {Your owl wants to know why there are so many towers.|Your owl has strong opinions about the library.|Your owl keeps falling asleep, standing up.}
text [fabd5c] = {驭兽学 II 的兽语课。小猫头鹰们得学会送信的路线。布拉斯克递给你一只，说：“把城堡给它讲清楚。”|又一只小猫头鹰，又是同一座城堡要讲。|又一只猫头鹰。你如今有一套讲稿，还在梁上刻了张地图。} {你的猫头鹰想知道为什么塔有这么多座。|你的猫头鹰对图书馆有很强烈的看法。|你的猫头鹰总是站着就睡着了。}
# en: A student in a stable loft with a young owl on their arm, pointing out of a high window toward a distant tower.
scene [3d64bf] = 马厩阁楼里，一名学生手臂上停着一只小猫头鹰，正指着高窗外远处的一座塔。
# en: Explain it in owl
opt.left.label [27c58e] = 用猫头鹰的话讲
# en: {You describe the castle in winds, perches and mice. The owl blinks, and goes and comes back with Brask's letter.|It takes a while to get "left" across to a bird. When it does, the owl does the route twice to show off.|You give your speech, map and all. The sleepy owl wakes for the important part and does the route without a mistake.}
opt.left.say.1 [42dfb9] = {你用风、栖木和老鼠来描述城堡。猫头鹰眨眨眼，飞出去，带回了布拉斯克的信。|要让一只鸟明白“左”可得花点工夫。等它明白了，它把路线飞了两遍来炫耀。|你讲完你那套说辞，连地图也用上了。打瞌睡的猫头鹰在关键处醒了过来，一处没错地飞完了路线。}
# en: {The owl listens closely, then flies to the kitchens. Every time.|The owl makes you explain "tower" seven times and then goes to sleep on your head.|Your owl sleeps through the whole speech, then wakes and flies to the kitchens. You're starting to take it personally.}
opt.left.say.2 [2c3a4c] = {猫头鹰听得很认真，然后飞去了厨房。每一次都是。|猫头鹰让你把“塔”解释了七遍，然后在你头上睡着了。|你的猫头鹰整篇说辞都在睡觉，醒来就飞去了厨房。你开始觉得这是针对你了。}
# en: Walk the route with it
opt.right.label [beabeb] = 带它走一遍路线
# en: {You walk the whole post route with the owl on your arm, up every stair. Your legs ache and the owl has learned it.|Up and down the castle with an owl on your wrist. People stare. The owl stares back.|You walk the route with the owl asleep on your arm. It learns it anyway, somehow. Brask says they do that.}
opt.right.say.1 [c28df0] = {你让猫头鹰停在手臂上，把整条送信路线走了一遍，每段楼梯都爬了。你腿疼，它学会了。|胳膊上架着一只猫头鹰，在城堡里上上下下。人们盯着看。猫头鹰盯回去。|你走着那条路线，猫头鹰在你胳膊上睡着了。可它还是学会了。布拉斯克说它们就是这样。}

@event beast_hooves
# en: Hoof Day
title [dcf707] = 修蹄日
# en: {Advanced Beastcraft does the work nobody else wants. Today it's hooves. A hippogriff's need trimming each month, and the hippogriff disagrees.|Hoof day. The stall is the same; the hippogriff's opinion is too.|Hooves. You go in with a bucket of apples and a plan.} {Today's hippogriff is grey and patient.|Today's is young and very sure of itself.|Today's is old and wants to tell you about it.}
text [61631e] = {高等驭兽学干的是没人想干的活。今天是修蹄。鹰头马身有翼兽的蹄子每月要修一次，而它们不同意。|修蹄日。马棚还是那个马棚，它的意见也还是那个意见。|修蹄。你带着一桶苹果和一个计划进去。} {今天这只是灰色的，很有耐心。|今天这只很年轻，非常自以为是。|今天这只很老，想跟你聊聊。}
# en: A student crouched beside a hippogriff in a stall, a hoof trimming knife in hand, the hippogriff looking down with one sceptical eye.
scene [e931b9] = 一名学生蹲在马棚里一只鹰头马身有翼兽旁边，手里拿着修蹄刀，那只兽用一只怀疑的眼睛俯视着。
# en: Talk it into lifting a foot
opt.left.label [33c422] = 劝它抬起蹄子
# en: {It listens to your case and lifts a hoof with enormous dignity. Brask watches from the door and says nothing.|You talk it through every hoof. It sighs at you between each one, like a patient uncle.|The old hippogriff tells you about its youth for every hoof. You listen to all of it, and it lifts each foot when the story ends.}
opt.left.say.1 [067441] = {它听完你的理由，极有尊严地抬起一只蹄子。布拉斯克在门口看着，什么也没说。|你一只一只蹄子地跟它谈。每修完一只它就冲你叹口气，像个耐心的叔叔。|修每只蹄子时，老鹰头马身有翼兽都要讲一段它年轻时的事。你全听完了，每段故事讲完它就抬起一只脚。}
# en: {It lets you get all the way to the last hoof before stepping on your foot.|It hears you out, then sits on you. Brask lifts it off with one hand and a word.|The old one talks and talks and doesn't lift a foot. You've been had, and Brask is laughing at the door.}
opt.left.say.2 [54f491] = {它一直等到你修最后一只蹄子，才踩了你的脚。|它听你说完，然后坐在了你身上。布拉斯克一只手加一句话就把它挪开了。|那只老的说个不停，就是不抬脚。你被耍了，布拉斯克在门口笑。}
# en: Rope, and Brask holding
opt.right.label [34c6c0] = 上绳子，请布拉斯克按着
# en: {The old way, then. A rope, a strong arm, Brask at its head. It's sweaty work and nobody enjoys it, including the hippogriff.|With Brask holding the head and you holding on, you finish every hoof. Your shoulders will remember it.|Apples first, then rope, then Brask. The plan works, and the hippogriff eats the plan.}
opt.right.say.1 [278161] = {老办法：一根绳，一条有力的胳膊，布拉斯克按着它的头。又累又满身汗，谁都不喜欢，包括那只兽。|布拉斯克按着头，你死死抓着，每只蹄子都修完了。你的肩膀会记住这一天。|先给苹果，再上绳子，再叫布拉斯克。计划成功了，鹰头马身有翼兽把计划也吃了。}

@event beast_night_stable
# en: Sitting Up With the Sick
title [789593] = 守着病兽
# en: {Advanced students take turns sitting up in the stables when a creature is ill. At the morning lecture Brask hands you a lantern, a blanket and a list for tonight.|Your name is on Brask's night-watch list again, and the list is shorter.|Night watch again tonight. Brask hands over the lantern without a word; the owls will only mutter.} {This time it's the griffon chick, off its food.|This time it's an old owl with a cough.|This time it's a hippogriff who ate something it shouldn't.} {season == "winter": The stable will be cold enough to see your breath.|At least it's warm in the straw.}
text [bc241e] = {有生物生病时，高年级生轮流在马厩守夜。早课上，布拉斯克交给你一盏灯笼、一条毯子和今晚的清单。|布拉斯克的守夜名单上又有你，清单短了些。|今晚又守夜。布拉斯克一言不发地把灯笼递给你；猫头鹰们只会嘀咕几声。} {这次是不肯吃东西的狮鹫雏鸟。|这次是一只咳嗽的老猫头鹰。|这次是一只吃了不该吃的东西的鹰头马身有翼兽。} {season == "winter": 马厩会冷得能看见自己的呼气。|至少干草堆里很暖和。}
# en: A student sitting in straw by lantern light, a sick creature curled beside them, the rest of the stables asleep.
scene [88ac60] = 一名学生借着灯笼光坐在干草里，一只生病的生物蜷在身旁，马厩里其余的一切都睡着了。
# en: Sit up all night
opt.left.label [464a6d] = 守它一整夜
# en: {You don't sleep, and by dawn it's breathing easier. Brask finds you asleep in the straw and leaves you there.|You watch it all night, changing the water and the straw. In the morning it eats, and so do you, enormously.|You sit up with the hippogriff while it groans about its mistake. By dawn it's eating again, and you're asleep against its side.}
opt.left.say.1 [2d3b38] = {你一夜没睡，天亮时它呼吸顺畅了些。布拉斯克发现你睡在干草里，就让你接着睡。|你看了它一整夜，换水，换干草。早上它吃东西了，你也吃了，吃了很多。|你守着那只为自己吃错东西而呻吟的鹰头马身有翼兽。天亮时它又开始吃东西了，你靠着它的身子睡着了。}
# en: Ask it where it hurts
opt.right.label [b5e61b] = 问它哪里疼
# en: {It tells you, in its own way, exactly where it hurts. You write it on Brask's list and both of you sleep.|It points with its whole body. You bring the right tonic and it drops off before the lantern does.|It tells you exactly what it ate, with some pride. You fetch the purge and it forgives you by morning.}
opt.right.say.1 [0f5834] = {它用自己的方式准确地告诉了你哪里疼。你写在布拉斯克的清单上，你们俩都睡了。|它用整个身子指给你看。你拿来对的补剂，它比灯笼先睡着。|它带着几分得意，一五一十地告诉你吃了什么。你取来了催吐药，早上它就原谅了你。}
# en: {It tells you a great deal, about its neighbours, the hay and the moon, and nothing about where it hurts.|It won't talk to you. It talks to the lantern. You stay up anyway, which is the point.|It won't say what it ate, out of embarrassment. You guess, and Brask corrects the guess in the morning.}
opt.right.say.2 [23dbdb] = {它跟你讲了很多，关于邻居、干草和月亮，就是没讲哪里疼。|它不跟你说话。它跟灯笼说话。你还是守着，这才是要点。|出于难为情，它不肯说吃了什么。你猜了一个，第二天早上布拉斯克纠正了你的猜测。}
# en: Speak with it properly
opt.up.label [70fe7d] = 好好跟它说说话
# en: {With the spell, it's easy. It explains the pain, the food, and what it thinks of the night. You fetch the right remedy.|You speak properly, and it answers properly, slowly, like someone who's been waiting. You both feel better.|You ask it properly and it tells you, ashamed, what it ate. The remedy is simple. The lecture you give it is not.}
opt.up.say.1 [68b3c8] = {有了咒语就容易了：它讲了疼在哪儿，吃了什么，还有它对这一夜的看法。你取来了对的药。|你好好地说，它也好好地答，慢慢的，像等了很久的人。你们俩都好受些了。|你好好地问，它羞愧地说出了吃了什么。药很简单。你给它上的那一课可不简单。}

@event umbral_ward_candle
# en: Ward the Candle
title [b4ebd5] = 护住蜡烛
# en: {Ward at Umbral Theory II. Ward a candle while your partner tries to put it out. Today that's {partner}.|Candle wards again, and the lamps are lower. {partner} is across the bench.|The candle exercise. You're paired with {partner}, who rolls up {their} sleeves.} {The professor walks between the benches with a hand over the flames.|The room smells of wax and burnt thread.|Someone's ward has shrunk to the size of a thimble.}
text [294dde] = {暗影理论 II 的护界课。给一根蜡烛设下护界，同时你的搭档设法把它弄灭。今天的搭档是{partner}。|又是蜡烛护界，灯压得更低了。{partner}坐在桌子对面。|蜡烛练习。你和{partner}一组，{they}卷起了{their}袖子。} {教授在桌间走动，一只手从火焰上方掠过。|屋里一股蜡和烧焦线头的味道。|有人的护界缩得只有顶针大小。}
# en: Two students at a dim bench under low lamps, a candle between them inside a faint pale shell, one student trying to blow it out.
scene [5a828b] = 低垂的灯下，两名学生坐在昏暗的长桌前，中间一根蜡烛罩在一层淡淡的苍白外壳里，其中一人正试图把它吹灭。
# en: A thick, honest shell
opt.left.label [53a438] = 一层厚实老实的壳
# en: {Your ward is plain and solid. {partner} blows and blows and the candle doesn't even lean.|Strong and dull. {partner} gives up and the two of you watch the flame burn down.|Your shell is thick and calm. {partner}'s sleeves are rolled for nothing; the flame doesn't even notice {them}.}
opt.left.say.1 [d60e26] = {你的护界朴素而结实。{partner}吹了又吹，蜡烛连歪都没歪。|结实而乏味。{partner}放弃了，你们俩一起看着火焰燃尽。|你的护界又厚又沉稳。{partner}白卷了袖子，火苗根本没注意到{them}。}
# en: A ward that turns them aside
opt.right.label [6b490b] = 设个把人引开的护界
# en: {Your ward turns {partner}'s breath round, and it blows {their} own hair into {their} eyes. The professor stops and says, "Ah."|{partner} reaches for your candle and finds {their} hand on the wrong side of the bench. The professor approves.|Your ward turns {partner} aside so gently that {they} try{s} three times before working out what happened.}
opt.right.say.1 [156f4c] = {你的护界把{partner}的气息拐了个弯，吹得{their}头发糊了一脸。教授停下脚步，说：“啊。”|{partner}伸手去够你的蜡烛，却发现自己的手到了桌子另一边。教授表示赞许。|你的护界把{partner}引开得如此轻柔，{they}试了三次才弄明白是怎么回事。}
# en: {Your clever ward turns aside the wrong thing, and the candle goes out with a smug little puff. {partner} smirks.|The ward bends {partner}'s breath straight into your face. You sneeze and the candle goes out.|Your ward shrinks to a thimble, like your neighbour's, and {partner} pinches the flame out with two fingers.}
opt.right.say.2 [1f1f04] = {你那个聪明的护界引开了错的东西，蜡烛得意地“噗”一声灭了。{partner}偷笑。|护界把{partner}的气息直直拐到你脸上。你打了个喷嚏，蜡烛灭了。|你的护界缩成了顶针大小，跟邻座的一样，{partner}两根手指就把火苗捏灭了。}
# en: A true ward
opt.up.label [720236] = 真正的护盾
# en: {You cast the real thing, the spell itself, and the candle sits inside a pale shell that hums. {partner} blows, then laughs, then asks you to show {them} how.|You raise the true ward. The professor stops at your bench and holds a hand over it, and for once says nothing at all.|The true ward comes easily now. {partner} tries everything, a breath, a book, a wet finger, and the flame burns on, untroubled.}
opt.up.say.1 [851c6a] = {你施出了真正的咒语，蜡烛被罩在一层嗡嗡作响的淡色护壳里。{partner}吹了又吹，然后笑了，然后请你教{them}。|你升起真正的护盾。教授在你桌前停下，把手悬在上面，难得一句话也没说。|真正的护盾现在来得毫不费力。{partner}什么都试了，吹气、书本、沾湿的手指，火苗依旧安然燃烧。}

@event umbral_dark_roll
# en: Who Moved
title [133ff8] = 谁动了
# en: {Umbral Theory II. The professor puts out every lamp, and in the dark one student moves. Say who, and where to.|Lamps out. You've learned to hear a sleeve.|The dark. You know the room's sounds, and which floorboard is a liar.} {Rain on the tower roof makes it harder.|It's so quiet you can hear the stair breathing.|Somebody's stomach rumbles, which helps no one.}
text [37cfa1] = {暗影理论 II。教授熄掉每一盏灯，黑暗中有一个学生会移动。说出是谁，挪到了哪里。|灯灭了。你已经学会听见一只袖子的声音。|黑暗。你熟悉这间屋子的声音，也知道哪块地板会撒谎。} {雨打在塔顶，让这更难了。|安静得能听见楼梯在呼吸。|有人肚子咕咕叫，这对谁都没帮助。}
# en: A pitch-dark classroom at the top of a tower, a few vague shapes of students sitting perfectly still in the gloom.
scene [d2fcaa] = 塔顶一间漆黑的教室，几个模糊的学生身影一动不动地坐在昏暗里。
# en: Listen, and name them
opt.left.label [80bc08] = 听，然后说出名字
# en: {"Third bench, to the window." Right. The professor relights a lamp and moves on.|You get it on the second try, by the creak of a bench and a faint smell of soap.|"Second bench, toward the door, stepping over the liar." The professor laughs in the dark, once.}
opt.left.say.1 [8cf4b3] = {“第三排，往窗边去了。”对了。教授重新点亮一盏灯，继续下一轮。|第二次你猜中了，靠的是一张长凳的吱呀声和一丝淡淡的肥皂味。|“第二排，往门那边去，跨过了那块说谎的地板。”教授在黑暗中笑了一声。}
# en: Be the one who moves
opt.right.label [25e0c1] = 做那个移动的人
# en: {You cross the whole room in the dark and nobody names you. When the lamps come up you're behind the professor.|Nobody hears you. The professor says, "Someone moved," and seems pleased not to know who.|You step over the floorboard that lies and cross the room in silence. Even the professor guesses wrong.}
opt.right.say.1 [9ff72e] = {你在黑暗中穿过整个房间，没人叫出你的名字。灯亮起时你站在教授身后。|没人听见你。教授说：“有人动了，”似乎很高兴自己不知道是谁。|你跨过那块会说谎的地板，悄无声息地穿过房间。连教授都猜错了。}
# en: {You catch a desk with your shin. "Window, limping," says everyone at once.|Your shoe squeaks on the second step, you turn your ankle stopping, and the whole class names you, with feeling.|You avoid the liar and find a new one. The whole room names you before you've reached the wall.}
opt.right.say.2 [a666e1] = {你的小腿撞上了桌子。“窗边，瘸着腿，”所有人异口同声。|你的鞋在第二级台阶上吱了一声，急停时还崴了脚。全班带着感情叫出了你的名字。|你避开了那块说谎的地板，却踩上了一块新的。还没走到墙边，全屋就叫出了你的名字。}

@event umbral_corridor_step
# en: Across the Corridor
title [d8d8cf] = 穿过走廊
# en: {Advanced Umbral Theory. Shadowstep across the corridor, door to door, the farthest the professor allows. "Short distances only," the professor says. "This is as short as long gets."|The corridor. The cold in between is colder than last time.|You stand at the door with your heels on the line. You know the cold that's coming.} {The lamps are out on the landing.|A draught is moving along the floor.|Someone came back from it with frost on one shoulder.}
text [09146d] = {高等暗影理论。用影步穿过走廊，从这扇门到那扇门，这是教授允许的最远距离。“只能短距离，”教授说，“这已经是短里面最长的了。”|走廊。中间的寒冷比上次更冷。|你脚跟抵着线站在门口。你知道将要袭来的那股寒意。} {楼梯平台上的灯灭了。|一股穿堂风贴着地面流动。|有人回来时一边肩膀上结着霜。}
# en: A dim stone corridor at the top of a tower, a student half stepping out of the shadow of one doorway while their own shadow lingers in another across the hall.
scene [e52a16] = 塔顶一条昏暗的石砌走廊，一名学生半个身子正从一扇门的阴影里跨出，而他们自己的影子还逗留在走廊对面的另一扇门里。
# en: Step across
opt.left.label [894fac] = 一步跨过去
# en: {One shadow, cold and long, and then the other. You come out on the far side shaking and grinning.|You step in by one door and out by the other, with a breath of frost on your collar. The professor writes your name, and a time.|You step into the cold you knew was coming and out the far door with nothing on your shoulder. The professor writes a shorter time.}
opt.left.say.1 [63de51] = {一片影子，又冷又长，然后是另一片。你从对面出来，浑身发抖，咧着嘴笑。|你从一扇门进，从另一扇门出，衣领上带着一口霜气。教授写下你的名字和一个时间。|你踏进早知会来的寒冷，从远处的门出来，肩上什么也没沾。教授写下了一个更短的时间。}
# en: {The cold in between is longer than you thought. You come out in the right doorway and can't feel your hands for an hour.|You step and come out in the same doorway you went in by, with the feeling that something looked at you on the way.|You come back with frost on one shoulder, like the others. It takes until supper to melt, and it isn't only cold.}
opt.left.say.2 [78743d] = {中间的寒冷比你想的更长。你从对的门口出来，一个钟头手都没有知觉。|你跨了一步，却从进去的那扇门出来了，总觉得路上有什么东西看了你一眼。|你像别人一样，回来时一边肩膀上结了霜。一直到晚饭才化，而且不只是冷。}
# en: Walk it, counting shadows
opt.right.label [de4a9d] = 走过去，数着影子
# en: {You walk the corridor and count every shadow and every lamp. The professor calls this "mapping your road".|You pace it out and write down each shadow's depth. Next time you'll step it. Probably.|You walk it and count the shadows, again. They're the same as last time, which you now realise is the lesson.}
opt.right.say.1 [e6a1e7] = {你走过走廊，数清每一片影子和每一盏灯。教授称之为“给你的路画地图”。|你一步步量过去，记下每片影子的深浅。下次你会用影步。大概吧。|你又走了一遍，数着影子。它们和上次一样，你这才明白这正是这一课。}
# en: Step with a held breath
opt.up.label [1d6b25] = 屏住呼吸踏影
# en: {You step without thinking about it, the way the spell knows. The cold barely touches you.|The spell takes you over quick and clean. Your fingers are cold for a minute.|You hold your breath and step. No frost, no cold, no time at all. The professor stops writing.}
opt.up.say.1 [207e6c] = {你不假思索地一步跨过，就像咒语本身知道路。寒意几乎没碰到你。|咒语带着你又快又干净地过去了。你的手指冷了一分钟。|你屏住呼吸，迈步。没有霜，没有冷，几乎没用时间。教授停下了笔。}

@event umbral_unpick_ward
# en: Unpicking the Box
title [be7a63] = 拆箱上的护界
# en: {Advanced Umbral Theory. The professor wards a small box and you unpick the ward without it noticing. "A ward that notices you," the professor says, "tells someone."|Box day. The professor has a new box, and a new ward on it.|The box. You've got a favourite needle for this now.} {This ward is fine as a cobweb.|This ward is thick and patient.|This ward hums when you breathe on it.}
text [7eb3d9] = {高等暗影理论。教授给一只小箱子设下护界，你要在它察觉不到的情况下把护界拆掉。“察觉到你的护界，”教授说，“会告诉别人。”|拆箱日。教授拿来一只新箱子，上面是新的护界。|箱子。你现在有一根专门用来干这个的针了。} {这道护界细得像蛛网。|这道护界又厚又有耐心。|你对它呼气时，这道护界会嗡嗡作响。}
# en: A small iron-bound box on a bench under a dim lamp, faint threads of a pale ward wrapped around it, a student leaning close with a needle.
scene [b89192] = 昏暗灯下的长桌上放着一只铁箍小箱，淡淡的苍白护界丝线缠绕着它，一名学生拿着针凑近。
# en: Thread by thread
opt.left.label [085b9e] = 一根一根地拆
# en: {An hour with a needle and a steady breath, and the box opens. The professor checks the ward and it has no idea.|You undo it strand by strand. It takes the whole lesson, and you don't look up once.|Your favourite needle and a slow breath. The humming ward goes quiet one strand at a time, and never notices it's gone.}
opt.left.say.1 [0fc048] = {一根针，一口稳稳的气，一个钟头后箱子开了。教授检查护界，它浑然不觉。|你一缕一缕地解开它。这花了整节课，你一次头都没抬。|你最顺手的那根针，一口慢慢的气。嗡鸣的护界一缕一缕地安静下来，始终没发觉自己已经没了。}
# en: Cut it in one stroke
opt.right.label [bb2609] = 一刀切断
# en: {You find the knot and cut it clean. The ward never knows. The professor raises a brow and opens the box.|One cut and the threads fall away. The professor spends a moment looking at the box and then at you.|You cut it between hums. The ward stops mid-note and never starts again. The professor writes something down.}
opt.right.say.1 [bd0b78] = {你找到结，干净利落地切断。护界始终没察觉。教授挑了挑眉，打开了箱子。|一刀下去，丝线纷纷散落。教授看了箱子一会儿，又看了看你。|你在两声嗡鸣之间下刀。护界在半个音上停住，再也没响起。教授记了点什么。}
# en: {The ward notices, snaps across your knuckles and rings like a little bell. The professor says, "And now someone knows." Everyone looks at you.|The ward snaps back at your hand and stings. The box stays shut.|You cut it mid-hum. It shrieks instead, and the professor has to open the window to let the sound out.}
opt.right.say.2 [ba15c0] = {护界察觉了，啪地抽过你的指节，像一只小铃铛一样响起来。教授说：“现在有人知道了。”所有人都看向你。|护界弹回来蜇了你的手。箱子还是关着。|你在嗡鸣中途下刀。它尖叫起来，教授只好开窗把声音放出去。}
